Copied: the 20 files below and nothing else of Bouncy Castle: Argon2BytesGenerator and Argon2Parameters, the BLAKE2b
digest they use, and the interfaces, exceptions and helpers those need to compile. No security provider, no JCA class.
Only core's backup/BackupKdf.kt uses them (ProcessIsolationTest).

What Robot changed:
- The package: org.bouncycastle became app.heyrobot.thirdparty.bouncycastle (its package and import lines), so the copy
  never meets a Bouncy Castle library another part of the build carries (Robolectric's, in the app's tests, is a
  signed jar whose packages can't take other classes).
- Each file starts with a comment naming where it came from, above its package line.
- Blake2bDigest.java: the three CryptoServicesRegistrar.checkConstraints(...) calls in its constructors and the import
  of CryptoServicesRegistrar are removed. They report a digest's use to Bouncy Castle's services registry, which
  would bring most of the library with it; they change no output.

